### Production hardening

| Area | Change |
|---|---|
| **Selection aliases** | Domain-aware normalization in `compatibility.py` so script `gemini` stays canonical while storyboard `gemini` → `gemini_ws` |
| **Settings v2** | Stored `selected_provider` values are rewritten to canonical ids on upgrade |
| **Node migrations M1–M3** | Wire aliases (`webhook`, `grok`, `kie-ai`, …) become canonical `provider_id`s |
| **Archives** | Re-redact workflow + execution JSON at pack time (egress surface) |
| **Notifications** | Channel errors go through `sanitize_message` |
| **Scheduler logs** | Unhandled exceptions are scrubbed before logging |
| **Health** | `details` and `HealthResult` objects scrub secrets/paths |

### New tests

- **`tests/test_provider_compat_matrix.py`** — full matrix over aliases (§40.3), settings formats (§42), M1–M4, legacy request fields (§40.1), built-in templates, frozen artifact roots (§44)
- **`tests/test_provider_hardening.py`** — isolation of import/health/create/execute/shutdown failures; concurrent reload consistency; fuzz of malformed manifests/results/callbacks; secret egress across records, SSE, archives, notifications

